<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Quick Add: Contact.

     THE GEOMETRY, MEASURED ON THE DEVICE (20 Oct 2026), because this card is
     the one shape that does not fit the other nine:

       - the owner placed it at 108.7dp wide x 72dp tall - ONE launcher row,
         not two. That is 40dp of content height at the other cards' 16dp
         padding, and 40dp is not enough for an icon AND a two-line label
         (the label alone is about 31dp).
       - so this layout uses 8dp padding, which gives 56dp of content height:
         a 22dp icon, a 2dp gap, and the label's two lines fit with room to
         spare. The other nine cards keep their 16dp, because their 2-cell
         budget is derived from it (166dp cell - 32dp) and their content is
         four or five bands rather than two.

     THE ICON IS ABOVE THE LABEL, not beside it. Beside it, the label's column
     is 48.7dp at 16dp padding - and "Medication", the longest word on any of
     these three cards, is about 62dp at 12sp. It does not fit, and with
     breakStrategy="simple" a word wider than its line is broken at the
     character level: "Medicatio" / "n". That is the same mid-word break the
     Next Dose widget had.

     ICON: the app's OWN shortcut disc - a coloured circle with a white
     glyph and the app's plus badge - in the Contacts module's colour. The
     owner asked for the icons from the bottom-nav module tabs, and this is
     that artwork: the glyph inside the disc is the module's own mark, the
     same one the nav draws, and the disc is the app's shortcut convention
     (ic_shortcut_contact.xml and its siblings).

     It is 22dp rather than the 48dp that shipped on 20 Oct, which was
     "too big and behind text": at 48dp it did not fit the 40dp content box
     at all, so it was clipped top and bottom AND drawn across the label. -->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:id="@+id/widget_root"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:padding="8dp"
    android:background="@drawable/widget_background">

    <ImageView
        android:layout_width="22dp"
        android:layout_height="22dp"
        android:layout_gravity="top|center_horizontal"
        android:contentDescription="@null"
        android:src="@drawable/ic_widget_contact" />

    <!-- maxLines 2, not 1: this label is a STATIC string, so there is no
         fit() call and no fitter to shrink it - maxLines is the only control
         on whether it ellipsizes. At one line it read "Add Co..." on the
         device. Pinned by quickAddWidgetLabelGuard.test.js. -->
    <TextView
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="top|center_horizontal"
        android:layout_marginTop="24dp"
        android:gravity="center"
        android:text="Add Contact"
        android:textSize="12sp"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
        android:textStyle="bold"
        android:maxLines="2"
        android:ellipsize="end"
        android:breakStrategy="simple" />
</FrameLayout>
